1
00:00:24,466 --> 00:00:27,466
Vineyard tomorrow.
Be outside your dorm at 6 AM sharp.

2
00:00:27,933 --> 00:00:30,300
Is your name Yut or Simp?

3
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:34,400
Next time, don't smile at
that old man again, Boss.

4
00:00:34,933 --> 00:00:35,733
I'm jealous.

5
00:00:37,733 --> 00:00:39,533
I thought you said you didn't like me.

6
00:00:41,866 --> 00:00:44,017
Or are you just
too turned on to remember?"

7
00:00:45,048 --> 00:00:46,214
You're quite the smooth talker.

8
00:00:46,625 --> 00:00:48,491
So where do you want me to kiss you?

9
00:00:48,956 --> 00:00:49,756
Your upper lip...

10
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:52,150
or...

11
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:55,052
your lower lip?

12
00:01:08,190 --> 00:01:08,990
Wake up.

13
00:01:18,471 --> 00:01:19,600
I know you're awake.

14
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:20,369
Get up.

15
00:01:24,037 --> 00:01:25,537
Why are you up so early?

16
00:01:26,229 --> 00:01:27,197
It's already ten.

17
00:01:27,639 --> 00:01:28,844
That's not early anymore.

18
00:01:29,307 --> 00:01:31,734
Get up and take a shower.

19
00:01:34,778 --> 00:01:36,078
What's wrong with you, Boss?

20
00:01:37,875 --> 00:01:39,175
Why are you so grumpy?

21
00:01:40,937 --> 00:01:41,804
I'm not grumpy.

22
00:01:42,232 --> 00:01:43,198
You're the one...

23
00:01:43,532 --> 00:01:45,632
You left me hanging
like that last night...

24
00:01:47,837 --> 00:01:48,637
What do you mean?

25
00:01:51,137 --> 00:01:52,548
Hanging?

26
00:01:54,089 --> 00:01:55,460
What kind of hanging?

27
00:01:58,286 --> 00:01:59,819
That's not what I meant.

28
00:02:02,965 --> 00:02:06,898
Okay, I'll wait until another time.

29
00:02:10,309 --> 00:02:14,675
Or do you want your naughty task
first thing in the morning?

30
00:02:21,671 --> 00:02:24,837
Get up and shower.
We still have work to do.

31
00:02:25,625 --> 00:02:27,858
Think carefully before you answer.

32
00:02:28,863 --> 00:02:29,863
Thitinant!

33
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:31,517
Get up.

34
00:02:31,517 --> 00:02:33,483
I'll give you one more chance.

35
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:36,550
Go take a shower!

36
00:02:51,271 --> 00:02:52,171
Thitinant!

37
00:02:56,644 --> 00:02:57,511
I'm going.

38
00:04:18,616 --> 00:04:21,424
These grapes have
been specially selected.

39
00:04:22,623 --> 00:04:24,071
They're very sweet.

40
00:04:24,813 --> 00:04:28,073
Well, I doubt they're
as sweet as you, Ms. Chat.

41
00:04:30,049 --> 00:04:32,019
Let's talk about the figures instead.

42
00:04:32,704 --> 00:04:36,187
We can discuss the taste during
the production trial.

43
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:45,002
I've already taken detailed notes

44
00:04:45,002 --> 00:04:46,649
on all the grape varieties.

45
00:04:54,982 --> 00:04:55,782
Oh!

46
00:04:56,482 --> 00:04:57,616
An insect, Ms. Chat.

47
00:04:58,049 --> 00:04:59,382
Let me shoo it away.

48
00:05:01,516 --> 00:05:02,316
Young lady.

49
00:05:02,316 --> 00:05:03,049
Yes?

50
00:05:03,049 --> 00:05:04,716
If you have nothing work-related to do,

51
00:05:05,282 --> 00:05:06,816
you can wait outside.

52
00:05:07,316 --> 00:05:08,116
Of course I do.

53
00:05:09,816 --> 00:05:12,003
A secretary has to stay
by her boss's side at all times.

54
00:05:12,517 --> 00:05:14,533
We can't afford to miss anything.

55
00:05:16,132 --> 00:05:17,516
Especially when it comes to insects.

56
00:05:18,049 --> 00:05:22,382
Your secretary really doesn't
make any sense.

57
00:05:27,316 --> 00:05:27,863
Does she?

58
00:05:28,948 --> 00:05:32,816
I think my secretary
is doing her job perfectly well.

59
00:05:36,682 --> 00:05:38,416
And I'm very pleased with her.

60
00:05:40,782 --> 00:05:42,682
Let's get back to business.

61
00:05:43,649 --> 00:05:44,982
As for the contract we discussed,

62
00:05:45,582 --> 00:05:47,182
I agree to the original terms.

63
00:05:50,249 --> 00:05:51,049
That's great, then.

64
00:05:52,249 --> 00:05:54,216
In that case, how about we...

65
00:05:56,616 --> 00:05:58,412
As for the details from here on,

66
00:05:58,812 --> 00:06:01,016
I'll have Mr. Karn take over.

67
00:06:01,382 --> 00:06:02,082
What?

68
00:06:02,082 --> 00:06:04,516
I think two men would
find it easier to work together.

69
00:06:05,582 --> 00:06:06,696
As for me,

70
00:06:07,039 --> 00:06:09,174
I probably won't be coming here to
oversee things in person anymore.

71
00:06:09,174 --> 00:06:11,682
But I hope this project
goes smoothly.

72
00:06:12,616 --> 00:06:13,606
And...

73
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:14,791
Nant.

74
00:06:15,248 --> 00:06:17,739
Pack your things. We're leaving.

75
00:06:18,649 --> 00:06:21,382
Ms. Chat, but I... Wait... I mean...

76
00:06:21,716 --> 00:06:24,416
Take care of your health, Unc.

77
00:06:25,616 --> 00:06:27,982
Especially when it comes to insects.

78
00:06:28,816 --> 00:06:30,882
Goodbye, Unc. Bye!

79
00:06:31,816 --> 00:06:34,649
But... Ms. Chat...Wait...

80
00:06:55,449 --> 00:06:56,582
It's only raining a little.

81
00:06:56,982 --> 00:06:58,582
My room is fine to sleep in,

82
00:06:59,416 --> 00:07:01,416
you didn't have to drag me over here.

83
00:07:05,816 --> 00:07:09,313
Far,and The roads might flood,
and traffic will be bad.

84
00:07:09,598 --> 00:07:11,419
I'm not driving you home tonight.

85
00:07:12,732 --> 00:07:16,396
So you're staying here.

86
00:07:21,216 --> 00:07:22,182
Don't be so suspicious.

87
00:07:23,116 --> 00:07:24,582
I'm not going to do anything to you.

88
00:07:33,316 --> 00:07:34,216
You won't do anything.

89
00:07:37,516 --> 00:07:39,582
But I'm not so sure about myself.

90
00:07:41,249 --> 00:07:42,382
I might do something.

91
00:07:53,782 --> 00:07:54,882
Then you sleep over there.

92
00:07:55,567 --> 00:07:56,578
I'll take the bed.

93
00:07:57,316 --> 00:07:59,777
And don't you dare come over here.

94
00:08:00,462 --> 00:08:01,463
Got it?

95
00:08:05,249 --> 00:08:06,049
Okay.

96
00:08:11,716 --> 00:08:12,816
Go take a shower.

97
00:08:13,716 --> 00:08:14,849
We've had a long day.

98
00:08:48,098 --> 00:08:49,065
Get a grip on yourself.

99
00:08:49,165 --> 00:08:49,965
Theerachat.

100
00:08:50,698 --> 00:08:51,498
Damn it.

101
00:08:54,565 --> 00:08:55,465
Stop thinking about it.

102
00:08:55,531 --> 00:08:56,331
Theerachat.

103
00:09:12,131 --> 00:09:14,231
What are you waiting for, Theerachat?

104
00:09:14,916 --> 00:09:18,839
Or are you hoping that girl
strips naked to seduce you again today?

105
00:09:20,323 --> 00:09:22,035
But what if...

106
00:09:26,365 --> 00:09:28,065
she actually comes over
like that again?

107
00:09:30,265 --> 00:09:31,065
Whoa!

108
00:09:31,431 --> 00:09:32,231
Whoa!

109
00:09:34,098 --> 00:09:35,765
Get a grip, Theerachat!

110
00:09:36,231 --> 00:09:38,531
Control yourself! Damn it!

111
00:09:41,431 --> 00:09:42,412
Don't think about it.

112
00:09:43,765 --> 00:09:44,621
Don't pay attention.

113
00:09:45,991 --> 00:09:48,371
Just keep repeating, "Sleep."

114
00:09:49,570 --> 00:09:52,003
Right, I have to ignore her.

115
00:09:52,631 --> 00:09:56,137
Sleep, sleep... Go to sleep.

116
00:09:59,731 --> 00:10:00,531
Sleep.

117
00:10:39,065 --> 00:10:40,165
Have you been waiting long?

118
00:10:41,298 --> 00:10:42,118
Who's waiting for you?

119
00:10:42,974 --> 00:10:44,421
I've been asleep for ages.

120
00:11:13,331 --> 00:11:14,965
Why are you tsking at me, Boss?

121
00:11:16,831 --> 00:11:17,698
Disappointed?

122
00:11:20,698 --> 00:11:21,498
No.

123
00:11:22,498 --> 00:11:24,331
It's just the rain.
It's annoying me.

124
00:11:28,965 --> 00:11:29,765
Oh, really?

125
00:11:30,831 --> 00:11:31,631
Yeah.

126
00:11:33,765 --> 00:11:35,698
I thought you were disappointed.

127
00:11:40,031 --> 00:11:42,265
Like you were waiting
for me to wear yesterday's lingerie.

128
00:11:45,065 --> 00:11:46,031
Sorry to disappoint you.

129
00:11:48,231 --> 00:11:49,665
It's just too cold in here tonight.

130
00:12:22,331 --> 00:12:23,831
Want to continue that kiss?

131
00:12:32,698 --> 00:12:35,698
No answer means you don't want to.

132
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:13,698
How am I supposed to sleep tonight?

133
00:13:15,031 --> 00:13:15,965
You little brat.

134
00:13:27,331 --> 00:13:28,431
So soft.

135
00:14:02,065 --> 00:14:02,865
Hey!

136
00:14:06,298 --> 00:14:08,765
Were you touching me
while I was asleep, Boss?

137
00:14:11,431 --> 00:14:12,665
You're quite naughty, aren't you?

138
00:14:15,265 --> 00:14:17,308
Are you crazy? Who touched you?

139
00:14:17,308 --> 00:14:20,531
I'm the one who should be asking you
why you're in my bed.

140
00:14:24,731 --> 00:14:26,431
The sofa was uncomfortable.

141
00:14:27,365 --> 00:14:28,865
And there's plenty of room on this bed.

142
00:14:29,165 --> 00:14:30,731
So I just moved over.

143
00:14:31,965 --> 00:14:33,065
I just didn't expect

144
00:14:34,931 --> 00:14:37,565
to wake up with my buttons undone.

145
00:14:43,031 --> 00:14:43,965
I didn't undo them.

146
00:14:44,631 --> 00:14:46,065
Your pajamas is old.

147
00:14:46,298 --> 00:14:47,498
The buttons must've come undone
by themselves.

148
00:14:48,431 --> 00:14:49,831
Don't accuse me!

149
00:15:12,265 --> 00:15:13,065
Sigh...

150
00:15:14,265 --> 00:15:16,831
I thought you wanted some milk
first thing in the morning.

151
00:15:20,065 --> 00:15:20,865
You perverted.

152
00:15:21,031 --> 00:15:23,365
Button your shirt right now.

153
00:15:23,731 --> 00:15:25,431
Then get off my bed.

154
00:15:27,031 --> 00:15:27,831
Get off!

155
00:15:29,031 --> 00:15:30,065
I don't know how to.

156
00:15:54,135 --> 00:15:56,135
Boss, between the milk in your hand

157
00:15:58,834 --> 00:16:00,834
and mine...

158
00:16:01,665 --> 00:16:03,165
which one looks more appetizing?

159
00:16:10,098 --> 00:16:11,931
Who would want to drink spoiled milk?

160
00:16:24,665 --> 00:16:25,698
Spoiled milk?

161
00:16:27,298 --> 00:16:28,098
Yeah.

162
00:16:30,431 --> 00:16:32,065
You really don't find it appetizing?

163
00:16:33,531 --> 00:16:34,331
No.

164
00:16:35,765 --> 00:16:38,898
No...not appetizing at all.

165
00:17:54,298 --> 00:17:55,744
This milk isn't spoiled.

166
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,783
It's even sweet.

167
00:18:31,865 --> 00:18:34,705
Nant, get down first.

168
00:18:38,472 --> 00:18:39,431
Someone's calling.

169
00:18:47,098 --> 00:18:48,065
It's Chom!

170
00:18:57,265 --> 00:18:58,331
Hello, Chat.

171
00:18:58,665 --> 00:18:59,465
Are you awake yet?

172
00:19:00,165 --> 00:19:01,065
Hello, Chom.

173
00:19:01,465 --> 00:19:03,031
Why are you calling so early?

174
00:19:04,865 --> 00:19:06,898
How did it end up looking like this?

175
00:19:08,031 --> 00:19:10,498
Hey! Why is your bed such a mess?

176
00:19:11,031 --> 00:19:12,898
You're usually such a neat freak.

177
00:19:16,831 --> 00:19:18,631
I was hungry, so I had some milk.

178
00:19:20,531 --> 00:19:23,531
Serious? Someone as strict as
you is eating on the bed?

179
00:19:24,165 --> 00:19:26,031
What's so strange about that?

180
00:19:26,731 --> 00:19:29,465
It's super weird.
Something's suspicious.

181
00:19:30,331 --> 00:19:32,631
Are you hiding someone in your room?

182
00:19:33,031 --> 00:19:33,831
Come on, tell me the truth.

183
00:19:34,231 --> 00:19:35,031
No.

184
00:19:35,331 --> 00:19:36,331
Are you crazy?

185
00:19:41,365 --> 00:19:43,165
Then whose stuff is that?

186
00:19:43,631 --> 00:19:44,431
Huh?

187
00:19:44,431 --> 00:19:45,231
What?

188
00:19:48,098 --> 00:19:48,898
The housekeeper's.

189
00:19:49,265 --> 00:19:50,265
You don't have a housekeeper.

190
00:19:51,065 --> 00:19:54,298
I just hired one yesterday.

191
00:19:56,931 --> 00:20:00,665
Do you think I wouldn't recognize
Nant's backpack?

192
00:20:01,098 --> 00:20:01,898
Ow!

193
00:20:03,565 --> 00:20:04,365
Ow.

194
00:20:05,131 --> 00:20:05,931
That hurts.

195
00:20:06,165 --> 00:20:06,965
Uh...

196
00:20:07,731 --> 00:20:08,831
The bed caught my leg.

197
00:20:09,231 --> 00:20:11,331
Nant, come out. I know you're there.

198
00:20:16,931 --> 00:20:17,898
Hello.

199
00:20:21,231 --> 00:20:24,565
Is this the milk
you were having in bed?

200
00:20:25,965 --> 00:20:26,765
Chom!

201
00:20:27,331 --> 00:20:28,383
Are you crazy?

202
00:20:28,383 --> 00:20:28,883
Hmm?

203
00:20:29,665 --> 00:20:30,498
It's not like that.

204
00:20:31,065 --> 00:20:32,031
It's really not like that.

205
00:20:32,431 --> 00:20:33,865
If it's not like that, then what is it?

206
00:20:34,365 --> 00:20:35,740
You're so cheeky.

207
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:36,240
Chom!

208
00:20:36,365 --> 00:20:37,165
You little brat.

209
00:20:38,098 --> 00:20:38,898
You!

210
00:20:39,165 --> 00:20:40,165
Go take a shower right now.

211
00:20:40,465 --> 00:20:41,631
And get dressed properly.

212
00:20:43,098 --> 00:20:43,898
Go!

213
00:20:44,365 --> 00:20:45,165
Hurry up!

214
00:20:48,565 --> 00:20:49,365
Go get dressed!

215
00:20:58,931 --> 00:21:00,365
What is your excuse now?

216
00:21:01,031 --> 00:21:01,531
Huh?

217
00:21:01,531 --> 00:21:03,298
There's really nothing going on. Ow!

218
00:21:03,531 --> 00:21:05,098
I'm hanging up now. I need to rest.

219
00:21:05,531 --> 00:21:06,731
Nothing going on, really?

220
00:21:07,165 --> 00:21:07,965
Ow!

221
00:21:08,131 --> 00:21:08,931
Well...

222
00:21:09,565 --> 00:21:12,524
It was late last night.

223
00:21:12,524 --> 00:21:15,093
And traffic was terrible.
There was no way home.

224
00:21:15,436 --> 00:21:18,041
So I just let her stay here.
That's all.

225
00:21:18,265 --> 00:21:19,151
That's all?

226
00:21:19,436 --> 00:21:22,550
You have so many rooms.
Why did you have to sleep together?

227
00:21:25,165 --> 00:21:28,284
I mean... We got back
and were already tired.

228
00:21:28,684 --> 00:21:31,425
I didn't think it through,
so I let her sleep on the sofa.

229
00:21:31,425 --> 00:21:34,065
There's really nothing going on.
Why are you so suspicious?

230
00:21:34,631 --> 00:21:37,135
Hmm. Nothing going on, really?

231
00:21:37,135 --> 00:21:40,365
You never let anyone into your condo.

232
00:21:41,065 --> 00:21:43,231
I told you there's nothing going on.
Then there's nothing going on, Chom.

233
00:21:43,665 --> 00:21:44,465
Ow!

234
00:21:44,465 --> 00:21:47,231
What's with all the questions?
I'm going to get some rest.

235
00:21:47,765 --> 00:21:48,565
Okay.

236
00:21:52,231 --> 00:21:54,586
Hello, Mom.
I've got big news!

237
00:21:54,586 --> 00:21:57,359
Remember how you told me
to keep an eye on Chat?

238
00:21:57,359 --> 00:21:58,698
I found something.

239
00:21:59,298 --> 00:22:00,098
What did you find?

240
00:22:00,498 --> 00:22:02,365
I found Nant in Chat's room.

241
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:04,720
Wait... Nant?
That secretary intern?

242
00:22:06,131 --> 00:22:09,684
Yes. Chat said they got back
late last night,

243
00:22:09,684 --> 00:22:11,621
so she let Nant stay over.

244
00:22:11,621 --> 00:22:13,498
But I think something's fishy.

245
00:22:14,431 --> 00:22:16,865
Could these two have known
each other before the wedding?

246
00:22:17,565 --> 00:22:18,965
What do you mean, Mom?

247
00:22:20,078 --> 00:22:25,606
I'm just guessing.
Chat might be planning something.

248
00:22:25,606 --> 00:22:28,015
Or that girl might be approaching her
for some reason.

249
00:22:28,765 --> 00:22:30,898
So what should I do next?

250
00:22:32,659 --> 00:22:34,659
Just keep doing what you're doing.
Watch them both.

251
00:22:34,659 --> 00:22:39,228
I'll have someone investigate
Nant's background.

252
00:22:39,228 --> 00:22:41,083
I want to know if this girl

253
00:22:41,197 --> 00:22:43,569
had any connection to Chat
before joining the company.

254
00:22:43,898 --> 00:22:47,431
Of course. I'll keep an eye on
their every move, Mom.

255
00:22:51,298 --> 00:22:54,231
And please send the details
to me by email, okay?

256
00:22:54,631 --> 00:22:55,431
Yes.

257
00:22:58,931 --> 00:23:01,294
Secretary Han, can I ask you something?

258
00:23:01,294 --> 00:23:02,098
Of course.

259
00:23:03,265 --> 00:23:06,831
Do you know why Chat came back from
the vineyard earlier than planned?

260
00:23:07,965 --> 00:23:11,731
Something must have
happened that upset her.

261
00:23:13,431 --> 00:23:15,498
Was Mr. Yut hitting on her too much?

262
00:23:17,131 --> 00:23:18,165
Something like that.

263
00:23:19,098 --> 00:23:22,588
By the way, what do you think?

264
00:23:22,588 --> 00:23:24,149
Do you think Chat and Nant

265
00:23:24,149 --> 00:23:26,631
are more than just boss
and subordinate?

266
00:23:28,431 --> 00:23:29,231
I don't think so.

267
00:23:31,131 --> 00:23:33,331
They're just getting closer,
that's all.

268
00:23:33,565 --> 00:23:35,465
Ever since they went to karaoke.

269
00:23:36,265 --> 00:23:37,065
How much closer?

270
00:23:37,665 --> 00:23:40,498
They switched to nicknames.

271
00:23:41,098 --> 00:23:41,898
That's it?

272
00:23:45,265 --> 00:23:48,606
Oh, here she comes.

273
00:23:48,606 --> 00:23:50,831
Why don't you ask her yourself, Chom?

274
00:23:51,331 --> 00:23:56,217
Hey, Nant fancy meeting you again.
We barely talked this morning.

275
00:23:57,073 --> 00:23:59,436
So, did you enjoy the vineyard?

276
00:24:01,965 --> 00:24:02,765
Uh...

277
00:24:04,565 --> 00:24:05,365
Nant.

278
00:24:06,665 --> 00:24:08,298
We were just there for work.

279
00:24:09,465 --> 00:24:10,631
How should I answer this?

280
00:24:11,065 --> 00:24:11,865
Uh...

281
00:24:14,165 --> 00:24:14,965
But...

282
00:24:18,298 --> 00:24:19,565
Everything went smoothly.

283
00:24:22,665 --> 00:24:23,698
Mr. Yut's wine

284
00:24:25,831 --> 00:24:26,698
was so delicious.

285
00:24:28,565 --> 00:24:30,765
And how was your trip back?

286
00:24:31,931 --> 00:24:32,731
Did you have fun?

287
00:24:33,665 --> 00:24:34,465
Huh?

288
00:24:37,931 --> 00:24:38,725
Chom.

289
00:24:40,438 --> 00:24:44,265
Since when do board members like you
conduct staff interviews themselves?

290
00:24:45,665 --> 00:24:50,131
I'm just curious. This morning,
I didn't even get to...

291
00:24:51,465 --> 00:24:52,740
If you want to know something about me,

292
00:24:53,311 --> 00:24:56,098
ask me directly.
Don't pressure my employees.

293
00:24:57,231 --> 00:25:01,631
Look at you, sticking up for her.

294
00:25:03,131 --> 00:25:06,098
Of course. She's my employee.

295
00:25:08,965 --> 00:25:11,865
Besides,
I don't like anyone disrupting work.

296
00:25:13,462 --> 00:25:14,263
Yes.

297
00:25:19,898 --> 00:25:20,698
As for you, Karn.

298
00:25:20,765 --> 00:25:21,265
Yes?

299
00:25:21,265 --> 00:25:21,965
Come here.

300
00:25:24,565 --> 00:25:25,898
About the banana project,

301
00:25:26,131 --> 00:25:29,331
have the team find suitable locations
and land for growing bananas.

302
00:25:29,831 --> 00:25:30,631
Understood.

303
00:25:31,698 --> 00:25:34,065
And have Nant compile everything
and send it to me as soon as possible.

304
00:25:34,698 --> 00:25:35,214
Yes.

305
00:25:35,214 --> 00:25:36,031
Understood?

306
00:25:36,531 --> 00:25:37,331
Understood.

307
00:25:38,365 --> 00:25:40,831
Nant, do you understand?

308
00:25:41,831 --> 00:25:43,465
Understood, Boss Chat.

309
00:27:11,265 --> 00:27:12,065
Nant.

310
00:27:15,965 --> 00:27:19,531
Nant, I've missed you.

311
00:27:21,865 --> 00:27:23,498
I've missed you too, Chat.

312
00:27:26,565 --> 00:27:29,565
Nant... I...

313
00:27:30,765 --> 00:27:32,265
Do you want to do it?

314
00:28:04,865 --> 00:28:06,165
You belong to me, Nant.

315
00:28:24,498 --> 00:28:26,782
(Nant's do the ringtone sound.)

316
00:29:07,831 --> 00:29:09,907
Oh, right.

317
00:29:10,535 --> 00:29:12,317
This is the banana processing project.

318
00:29:13,402 --> 00:29:15,779
I've compiled all the figures

319
00:29:16,750 --> 00:29:18,139
for the factory in Kamphaeng Phet.

320
00:29:18,824 --> 00:29:23,765
Also, Karn got all the details on
the banana land ready for you, Boss.

321
00:29:40,865 --> 00:29:42,865
What are you doing?

322
00:29:46,965 --> 00:29:48,631
I'm giving you a massage, Boss.

323
00:29:54,931 --> 00:29:58,631
Or would you rather do
something else instead?

324
00:30:03,865 --> 00:30:05,698
You're getting way
too good at teasing me.

325
00:30:09,331 --> 00:30:10,531
Thitinant.

326
00:30:14,165 --> 00:30:14,965
Uh...

327
00:30:55,831 --> 00:30:56,846
Sorry.

328
00:30:57,874 --> 00:30:58,928
You can go now.

329
00:30:59,613 --> 00:31:03,179
I'll review the land and
financial figures myself.

330
00:31:07,231 --> 00:31:08,498
Yes, Boss.

331
00:31:27,498 --> 00:31:30,065
Get a grip, Theerachat.

332
00:31:30,531 --> 00:31:31,765
Control yourself.

333
00:31:33,431 --> 00:31:36,331
If I keep this up, that girl is gonna
think I'm completely obsessed with her.

334
00:31:38,498 --> 00:31:39,631
It was just a dream.

335
00:31:43,231 --> 00:31:45,565
Where's Nant?

336
00:31:46,298 --> 00:31:49,025
Miss, please calm down.

337
00:31:49,025 --> 00:31:50,298
Can I help you with something?

338
00:31:50,631 --> 00:31:51,865
I'm looking for someone named Nant.

339
00:31:53,465 --> 00:31:56,526
I'm sorry, but
if this isn't work-related,

340
00:31:56,526 --> 00:31:58,601
please wait outside.

341
00:31:58,601 --> 00:31:59,731
I'll call Nant for you.

342
00:31:59,865 --> 00:32:00,454
No!

343
00:32:00,454 --> 00:32:01,879
I'll talk to her right here.

344
00:32:02,222 --> 00:32:03,974
Where the hell are you, Nant?

345
00:32:08,965 --> 00:32:09,965
I'm right here.

346
00:32:11,965 --> 00:32:14,631
Should I call security for you,
Nant?

347
00:32:15,698 --> 00:32:17,231
It's okay, Hanna.

348
00:32:25,265 --> 00:32:26,465
Do you remember me?

349
00:32:28,931 --> 00:32:30,165
Of course, Gam.

350
00:32:31,698 --> 00:32:33,431
Why don't we talk outside?

351
00:32:33,698 --> 00:32:34,931
Don't pretend to be shy.

352
00:32:35,465 --> 00:32:36,898
Let everyone know

353
00:32:37,298 --> 00:32:38,465
what you've done.

354
00:32:41,865 --> 00:32:43,531
What do you want?

355
00:32:44,898 --> 00:32:45,698
Because of you,

356
00:32:46,031 --> 00:32:48,265
my boyfriend left me.

357
00:32:48,931 --> 00:32:50,265
You ruined my life.

358
00:32:54,065 --> 00:32:55,632
Gam.

359
00:32:56,717 --> 00:32:58,975
Do you remember what
I told you that day?

360
00:33:00,802 --> 00:33:02,686
If you two truly loved each other,

361
00:33:03,765 --> 00:33:05,654
nothing could break you apart.

362
00:33:08,065 --> 00:33:09,665
I didn't make him leave you.

363
00:33:11,298 --> 00:33:12,365
I just said

364
00:33:12,898 --> 00:33:15,231
what your ex-boyfriend
didn't have the gut to say.

365
00:33:15,698 --> 00:33:16,765
But if it weren't for you,

366
00:33:17,831 --> 00:33:19,165
he'd still be with me.

367
00:33:20,498 --> 00:33:21,531
Gam.

368
00:33:23,631 --> 00:33:24,531
Since that day,

369
00:33:27,065 --> 00:33:29,531
has he ever texted you?

370
00:33:31,898 --> 00:33:32,765
Has he ever called?

371
00:33:33,298 --> 00:33:34,098
Has he ever text to...

372
00:33:35,331 --> 00:33:37,131
asked how you're doing?

373
00:33:40,265 --> 00:33:40,765
No, never.

374
00:33:42,135 --> 00:33:43,546
Then what am I supposed to do?

375
00:33:43,546 --> 00:33:45,624
Just accept that...

376
00:33:46,023 --> 00:33:47,297
he doesn't love me?

377
00:33:48,565 --> 00:33:49,207
No.

378
00:33:51,719 --> 00:33:54,065
I'm not saying you have
to accept it today.

379
00:33:56,265 --> 00:33:57,631
But even if he came back,

380
00:33:58,965 --> 00:34:00,731
his heart wouldn't be with you anymore.

381
00:34:02,231 --> 00:34:03,898
Would you really be happy like that?

382
00:34:21,531 --> 00:34:22,331
Here.

383
00:34:25,131 --> 00:34:26,098
Gam.

384
00:34:29,265 --> 00:34:30,931
You can be angry with me if you want.

385
00:34:32,731 --> 00:34:36,298
But trying to hold on to someone
whose heart is no longer in it...

386
00:34:37,465 --> 00:34:38,898
won't make you happy.

387
00:34:41,231 --> 00:34:47,098
Trust me. Take care of yourself
and move on.

388
00:35:00,098 --> 00:35:01,098
It's okay.

389
00:35:09,631 --> 00:35:10,431
I'm sorry.

390
00:35:13,098 --> 00:35:14,731
I'm sorry for causing a scene.

391
00:35:16,731 --> 00:35:17,565
I'm truly sorry.

392
00:35:18,865 --> 00:35:19,665
It's alright.

393
00:35:33,765 --> 00:35:34,765
Secretary Han.

394
00:35:35,131 --> 00:35:35,931
Uh...

395
00:35:36,265 --> 00:35:37,065
Yes, Boss?

396
00:35:38,298 --> 00:35:39,731
Push the meeting back
by fifteen minutes.

397
00:35:40,698 --> 00:35:41,498
Certainly.

398
00:35:42,265 --> 00:35:43,698
Go get ready for the meeting.

399
00:35:47,131 --> 00:35:48,845
And whoever recorded this,

400
00:35:48,845 --> 00:35:50,209
make sure they delete every clip.

401
00:35:51,122 --> 00:35:52,600
If any of this footage gets leaked,

402
00:35:53,513 --> 00:35:54,640
I won't let it slide.

403
00:35:58,731 --> 00:35:59,531
Boss...

404
00:36:00,165 --> 00:36:01,298
I'm sorry.

405
00:36:03,431 --> 00:36:05,465
I'm sorry for causing trouble
for the company.

406
00:36:06,431 --> 00:36:09,065
It's okay. You handled it well.

407
00:36:15,898 --> 00:36:17,331
Now go get ready for the meeting.

408
00:36:37,698 --> 00:36:39,365
I'm ready for the meeting, Boss.

409
00:36:42,365 --> 00:36:44,965
Are you okay after what happened?

410
00:36:46,631 --> 00:36:47,465
I'm fine.

411
00:36:48,898 --> 00:36:49,898
I handled it.

412
00:36:50,665 --> 00:36:52,698
It's something I had to
take responsibility for anyway.

413
00:36:54,231 --> 00:36:56,331
I thought you were going to slap her.

414
00:36:58,031 --> 00:36:59,565
Why would I slap her?

415
00:37:01,431 --> 00:37:02,298
Just kidding.

416
00:37:03,231 --> 00:37:06,431
But it's good you
didn't argue with her.

417
00:37:07,898 --> 00:37:11,208
What would arguing accomplish, Boss?

418
00:37:11,779 --> 00:37:15,574
She's heartbroken.
She wouldn't listen anyway.

419
00:37:19,431 --> 00:37:23,698
You're much better at handling people
than I expected.

420
00:37:28,731 --> 00:37:30,298
Thank you for the compliment.

421
00:37:33,098 --> 00:37:35,043
What compliment?
Who complimented you?

422
00:37:36,527 --> 00:37:39,260
I was just saying.

423
00:37:41,030 --> 00:37:46,179
Anyway, Nant, help me review
the factory production costs today.

424
00:37:51,331 --> 00:37:52,431
I'd be happy to, Boss.

425
00:37:58,665 --> 00:37:59,165
Boss.

426
00:38:01,677 --> 00:38:02,636
Tomorrow's Saturday.

427
00:38:04,235 --> 00:38:05,898
Do you have any plans?

428
00:38:07,265 --> 00:38:08,065
Why do you ask?

429
00:38:09,865 --> 00:38:14,231
Well... I was thinking of inviting you
to visit my grandparents.

430
00:38:16,231 --> 00:38:17,831
I haven't seen them in ages.

431
00:38:19,165 --> 00:38:20,131
I miss them so much.

432
00:38:22,531 --> 00:38:25,265
But when I think
about making the trip alone,

433
00:38:26,031 --> 00:38:28,765
I can't help thinking
of someone around here.

434
00:38:34,898 --> 00:38:36,898
Please come with me, Boss.

435
00:38:38,165 --> 00:38:43,531
You suddenly want to invite me
on a trip out of town?

436
00:38:47,965 --> 00:38:50,270
We could...uh...

437
00:38:53,010 --> 00:38:54,498
We could enjoy some fresh air.

438
00:38:55,698 --> 00:38:56,965
A change of scenery.

439
00:38:58,631 --> 00:38:59,431
Please?

440
00:38:59,965 --> 00:39:02,431
I want to introduce
you to my grandparents.

441
00:39:04,065 --> 00:39:04,865
Okay.

442
00:39:08,031 --> 00:39:10,165
I'm free, so why not?

443
00:39:22,465 --> 00:39:27,098
Go all out today. I'm treating you to a
birthday celebration for being single.

444
00:39:28,898 --> 00:39:29,931
Can we not talk about that?

445
00:39:30,298 --> 00:39:31,098
It's annoying.

446
00:39:31,365 --> 00:39:32,898
Is Chat not coming?

447
00:39:33,098 --> 00:39:34,265
Her friend just got dumped.

448
00:39:34,431 --> 00:39:35,731
Can't she even show up
to wish her happy birthday?

449
00:39:36,665 --> 00:39:37,965
She said she has a meeting.

450
00:39:38,365 --> 00:39:40,365
A meeting with her secretary,
apparently.

451
00:39:41,365 --> 00:39:43,865
Oh, someone's in love!

452
00:39:56,831 --> 00:40:00,296
It's so packed in here.
Do you think we'll even get a table?

453
00:40:00,296 --> 00:40:01,831
I'm starving.

454
00:40:02,831 --> 00:40:03,765
Yeah, seriously.

455
00:40:04,965 --> 00:40:07,031
Excuse me,
do you have any tables available?

456
00:40:07,331 --> 00:40:10,765
I'm sorry, but we're fully booked.

457
00:40:12,131 --> 00:40:15,065
Oh! Kirin Ham and Cheese.

458
00:40:17,865 --> 00:40:18,665
Ham and Cheese?

459
00:40:19,765 --> 00:40:21,531
That's such a ridiculous nickname.

460
00:40:22,498 --> 00:40:24,331
Come on, my table's still free.

461
00:40:24,631 --> 00:40:25,431
Come sit with us.

462
00:40:25,831 --> 00:40:27,165
It's okay. We don't want to impose.

463
00:40:27,731 --> 00:40:28,366
Come on, Yong!

464
00:40:28,366 --> 00:40:29,065
Wait!

465
00:40:29,365 --> 00:40:30,179
Let's eat here.

466
00:40:30,179 --> 00:40:31,098
Everywhere else is packed.

467
00:40:31,231 --> 00:40:32,083
I don't feel like going somewhere else.

468
00:40:32,083 --> 00:40:32,583
Come on!

469
00:40:33,298 --> 00:40:34,098
Let's sit!

470
00:40:36,098 --> 00:40:40,265
Hello, we were actually looking
for a table. Thanks for the invite.

471
00:40:40,765 --> 00:40:43,965
Please, make yourselves comfortable.

472
00:40:51,298 --> 00:40:53,331
Who is that woman?

473
00:40:54,031 --> 00:40:54,898
She's damn gorgeous.

474
00:40:56,498 --> 00:40:59,165
That's the OB-GYN I told you about.

475
00:40:59,631 --> 00:41:00,965
The one who stole my croissant

476
00:41:01,165 --> 00:41:03,065
and gave me an internal examination.

477
00:41:03,631 --> 00:41:04,431
Hey!

478
00:41:04,865 --> 00:41:05,731
This woman?

479
00:41:07,065 --> 00:41:07,865
Holy shit.

480
00:41:08,331 --> 00:41:09,131
She's gorgeous.

481
00:41:15,065 --> 00:41:16,731
Funny how we keep
running into each other.

482
00:41:18,165 --> 00:41:20,531
We must have had quite
a lot of karma together in a past life.

483
00:41:22,231 --> 00:41:26,765
Anyway, any trouble down there today?
Would you like another examination?

484
00:41:27,765 --> 00:41:29,620
I'm perfectly fine, Doc.

485
00:41:29,620 --> 00:41:31,165
No need to worry.

486
00:41:32,765 --> 00:41:37,331
Two minutes in and it's already
a war zone. Today’s gonna be wild.

487
00:41:40,765 --> 00:41:41,765
What would you ladies like to order?

488
00:41:45,831 --> 00:41:48,531
I'll have a mixed sauce platter
and an order of fries.

489
00:41:48,698 --> 00:41:49,498
Certainly.

490
00:41:50,631 --> 00:41:52,131
I was going to order fries too.

491
00:41:53,131 --> 00:41:55,265
Excuse me, could we get
another order of fries?

492
00:41:55,698 --> 00:41:58,231
Sorry, we can only serve
one order of fries.

493
00:42:01,298 --> 00:42:02,898
I ordered first.

494
00:42:05,665 --> 00:42:08,451
But since you're older,

495
00:42:08,451 --> 00:42:10,965
shouldn't you let the younger ones
have them?

496
00:42:12,065 --> 00:42:16,176
A rude little brat like you
doesn't deserve anyone's generosity.

497
00:42:16,176 --> 00:42:17,731
I ordered first.

498
00:42:18,020 --> 00:42:19,278
Wait, wait.

499
00:42:20,131 --> 00:42:26,131
Please give them to me.
I'm really hungry.

500
00:42:27,898 --> 00:42:31,431
Rin, do you have to lose your mind
over food every single time?

501
00:42:32,465 --> 00:42:34,698
Look at her!
Is she messing with me?

502
00:42:37,498 --> 00:42:39,265
Go on, hit her.

503
00:42:41,631 --> 00:42:45,465
Uh, how about we just serve
one medium plate for everyone to share?

504
00:42:46,331 --> 00:42:47,365
(Kirin) Sure.
(Dr. Ai) Sure.

505
00:43:01,831 --> 00:43:03,065
Here you go.

506
00:43:15,465 --> 00:43:16,265
You spilled them!

507
00:43:16,698 --> 00:43:17,565
I'm eating these!

508
00:43:18,931 --> 00:43:20,065
Hey! I grabbed this one first!

509
00:43:20,165 --> 00:43:20,931
I grabbed this one too!

510
00:43:20,931 --> 00:43:21,765
Why are you fighting over them?

511
00:43:21,831 --> 00:43:23,165
Why did you grab the same one as me?

512
00:43:23,265 --> 00:43:24,065
Because I grabbed it first!

513
00:43:24,098 --> 00:43:24,898
No, I did!

514
00:43:25,565 --> 00:43:26,365
I grabbed it first!

515
00:43:27,727 --> 00:43:30,031
That's your problem!
I'm taking this one.

516
00:43:30,031 --> 00:43:30,965
And I want this one!

517
00:43:37,883 --> 00:43:39,084
Ow!

518
00:43:41,810 --> 00:43:43,131
Hey!

519
00:43:43,131 --> 00:43:44,898
Don't back down if you don't have to.

520
00:43:45,386 --> 00:43:47,971
Bitch, stop it.
I'm embarrassed for them.

521
00:43:48,108 --> 00:43:50,000
(Yong) I'll buy you a new one.
(Kirin) Ugh, you're blocking me!

522
00:43:50,231 --> 00:43:51,734
This Doc has gone too far.

523
00:43:52,762 --> 00:43:53,937
She's already seen my insides once.

524
00:43:54,451 --> 00:43:55,558
I'm not backing down this time.

525
00:43:55,958 --> 00:43:58,431
What do you mean,
seen your insides, Ai?

526
00:43:59,331 --> 00:44:00,498
What are you doing to your patient?

527
00:44:01,031 --> 00:44:01,831
I didn't do anything.

528
00:44:02,331 --> 00:44:04,465
Why are you bringing up
what happened in the examination room?

529
00:44:04,731 --> 00:44:06,531
Do you really have to hold
a grudge over something so small?

530
00:44:07,298 --> 00:44:10,298
I wouldn't hold a grudge
if it were another doctor.

531
00:44:11,165 --> 00:44:13,498
But since it's you,
I'm not letting it go.

532
00:44:15,231 --> 00:44:17,631
Excuse me, one bottle of wine, please!

533
00:44:24,565 --> 00:44:25,665
Let's settle this
with a drinking contest.

534
00:44:26,331 --> 00:44:28,531
Let's see who wins, girl.

535
00:44:30,298 --> 00:44:32,422
Dr. Ai, don't stoop to her level.

536
00:44:32,422 --> 00:44:34,731
Her brain hasn't grown
as much as the rest of her.

537
00:44:34,865 --> 00:44:36,565
Bring it on! I'm not scared.

538
00:44:38,031 --> 00:44:41,131
Go ahead. I'm ready to pay
for your stomach pumping.

539
00:44:41,631 --> 00:44:43,531
Fine! I'm exhausted.

540
00:45:13,165 --> 00:45:13,965
Ow!

541
00:45:14,431 --> 00:45:15,231
Ow!

542
00:45:15,331 --> 00:45:15,965
You!

543
00:45:15,965 --> 00:45:17,865
Can't you let me win just once?

544
00:45:19,431 --> 00:45:20,231
No!

545
00:45:24,365 --> 00:45:25,020
So that's how you want to play?

546
00:45:25,020 --> 00:45:26,082
Yeah.

547
00:45:26,082 --> 00:45:26,582
What, now?

548
00:45:30,298 --> 00:45:31,665
Got a problem with that?

549
00:45:32,731 --> 00:45:34,665
You jerk!

550
00:45:35,665 --> 00:45:36,465
Just let it go.

551
00:45:36,631 --> 00:45:38,831
Hey! So you have to
get physical now?

552
00:45:40,065 --> 00:45:40,865
Uh...

553
00:45:42,565 --> 00:45:43,365
Are you hurt?

554
00:45:43,965 --> 00:45:45,331
I didn't mean to.

555
00:45:45,765 --> 00:45:46,898
Of course it hurts!
What a stupid question.

556
00:45:48,931 --> 00:45:49,731
Then...

557
00:45:51,831 --> 00:45:52,831
If that's all...

558
00:45:54,298 --> 00:45:55,898
Aren't you going to take
any responsibility for this?

559
00:45:56,131 --> 00:45:57,707
Come and treat my wound right now.

560
00:45:57,707 --> 00:45:58,631
Dr. Ai.

561
00:45:59,565 --> 00:46:01,831
You're really going to
let this kid treat your wound?

562
00:46:02,231 --> 00:46:03,365
Are you trying to get more wounded?

563
00:46:03,965 --> 00:46:05,531
You have to take
responsibility, don't you?

564
00:46:06,631 --> 00:46:07,965
Treat my wound right now.

565
00:46:28,231 --> 00:46:29,898
I treated your wound.
There, I took responsibility.

566
00:46:30,931 --> 00:46:31,765
Happy now?

567
00:46:32,731 --> 00:46:35,498
I asked you to treat my wound,
not kiss me, idiot!

568
00:46:37,098 --> 00:46:39,731
You told me to take responsibility!

569
00:46:41,098 --> 00:46:43,765
I didn't say you could kiss me like
this! You can't just go kissing people.

570
00:46:45,898 --> 00:46:47,065
Are you crazy?

571
00:46:47,698 --> 00:46:49,665
Let's go. I'm begging you.
Come on!

572
00:46:49,931 --> 00:46:50,731
Why are we leaving?

573
00:46:50,865 --> 00:46:51,665
Come on!

574
00:46:52,131 --> 00:46:54,898
Wait, you look familiar.

575
00:46:57,131 --> 00:47:00,031
Oh, I remember.
You're Chat's runaway groom, right?

576
00:47:02,231 --> 00:47:03,031
Yes, I am.

577
00:47:03,165 --> 00:47:04,265
Nice to meet you.

578
00:47:04,631 --> 00:47:05,865
I'm Chat's friend.

579
00:47:06,165 --> 00:47:07,665
My name's Jaokha. I'm a lawyer.

580
00:47:07,931 --> 00:47:09,365
If you ever want to sue Chat,

581
00:47:09,665 --> 00:47:10,731
you can contact me.

582
00:47:11,465 --> 00:47:13,065
I know plenty of her secrets.

583
00:47:13,831 --> 00:47:15,465
I guarantee you'll win.

584
00:47:17,065 --> 00:47:17,931
No, thank you.

585
00:47:19,965 --> 00:47:20,765
Let's go.

586
00:47:20,898 --> 00:47:22,898
Why do I keep randomly running
into all these weirdos?

587
00:47:23,031 --> 00:47:24,131
Come on, hurry up.

588
00:47:24,331 --> 00:47:25,365
We're not done yet.

589
00:47:26,065 --> 00:47:27,298
Don't let me catch you again, doc!

590
00:47:27,631 --> 00:47:29,031
Next time, I won't go easy on you!

591
00:47:29,131 --> 00:47:29,931
Bring it on!

592
00:47:29,965 --> 00:47:30,765
Hey!

593
00:47:31,098 --> 00:47:31,898
You.

594
00:47:32,931 --> 00:47:33,898
Sit down, sit down.

595
00:47:39,231 --> 00:47:42,165
So, that was a new experience, huh?

596
00:47:44,131 --> 00:47:46,431
Yeah, that was one hell of a birthday.

597
00:48:13,092 --> 00:48:14,242
This way.

598
00:48:21,631 --> 00:48:23,431
Oh, Nant! You're here already?

599
00:48:23,765 --> 00:48:24,565
Hello.

600
00:48:25,065 --> 00:48:27,031
Hello, sweetheart.

601
00:48:28,365 --> 00:48:29,331
Hello, Grandpa.

602
00:48:29,831 --> 00:48:31,165
Oh, hello.

603
00:48:31,931 --> 00:48:32,898
And who's this?

604
00:48:33,498 --> 00:48:35,231
Oh, she's my boss.

605
00:48:36,031 --> 00:48:38,831
Well, I missed you both, Grandpa
and Grandma, so we came to visit.

606
00:48:39,565 --> 00:48:40,365
We missed you too.

607
00:48:40,765 --> 00:48:43,631
That's right. So I brought my boss
along to meet you both.

608
00:48:44,231 --> 00:48:45,531
Okay, okay

609
00:48:45,731 --> 00:48:46,365
Oh.

610
00:48:46,365 --> 00:48:48,298
So, is Grandma cooking up there?

611
00:48:48,898 --> 00:48:53,331
Since she heard you were coming, she's
been stuck in the kitchen all moring.

612
00:48:54,650 --> 00:48:55,665
Oh.

613
00:48:56,131 --> 00:48:56,931
Hello, dear.

614
00:48:56,931 --> 00:48:58,698
Come on, come see who's here!

615
00:48:59,031 --> 00:49:00,931
Oh my goodness!
Grandma's little girl!

616
00:49:03,431 --> 00:49:04,231
Hey.

617
00:49:05,031 --> 00:49:05,831
Hello, Grandma.

618
00:49:06,031 --> 00:49:06,831
Hello, dear.

619
00:49:08,098 --> 00:49:10,831
Did you bring your girlfriend, Nant?

620
00:49:13,131 --> 00:49:14,131
She's so pretty.

621
00:49:14,565 --> 00:49:16,031
No, no, that's not it.

622
00:49:16,565 --> 00:49:19,731
This is Ms. Chat, my boss.

623
00:49:21,265 --> 00:49:23,765
I brought her here to visit our home.

624
00:49:24,053 --> 00:49:25,270
Oh, I see.

625
00:49:25,898 --> 00:49:30,631
So, is Nant a bad girl?
Does she ever give you a hard time?

626
00:49:31,465 --> 00:49:35,786
Not at all. Nant is such a lovely girl.
She's very good at her job, too.

627
00:49:35,786 --> 00:49:39,965
I'm the one troubling you two
by showing up at such short notice.

628
00:49:40,331 --> 00:49:41,131
Thank you for having me.

629
00:49:41,365 --> 00:49:44,209
Oh, you're no trouble at all, dear.

630
00:49:44,209 --> 00:49:49,365
Just the two of us live here, so it’s
really lively having everyone over.

631
00:49:50,465 --> 00:49:54,242
You must be tired from the drive.
Have something to drink first.

632
00:49:54,242 --> 00:49:59,065
I'll go finish cooking.
I'll come get you when it's all ready.

633
00:49:59,531 --> 00:50:03,731
Thank you, Grandma. But
I really feel bad for bothering you.

634
00:50:04,031 --> 00:50:06,311
Don't be silly. No need to feel bad.

635
00:50:06,311 --> 00:50:09,131
You're our very special guest.

636
00:50:09,931 --> 00:50:11,240
Make yourself at home.

637
00:50:11,240 --> 00:50:13,048
Even though
we're out in the middle of nowhere,

638
00:50:13,048 --> 00:50:15,931
you're always welcome here.

639
00:50:18,165 --> 00:50:21,298
Nant, why don't you show
Ms. Chat around?

640
00:50:22,531 --> 00:50:24,365
I'll call you when the food is ready.

641
00:50:24,931 --> 00:50:27,498
Everyone's in for
a real treat this time.

642
00:50:29,065 --> 00:50:32,331
Just go look around.
We'll carry your luggage.

643
00:50:32,465 --> 00:50:32,965
Yeah.

644
00:50:32,965 --> 00:50:33,465
Let's go!

645
00:50:33,465 --> 00:50:34,131
Are you sure?

646
00:50:34,231 --> 00:50:35,031
It's fine.

647
00:50:35,531 --> 00:50:36,665
Let's go, dear.

648
00:50:36,765 --> 00:50:38,165
You must be tired.
Go get some rest first.

649
00:50:38,331 --> 00:50:39,498
Come on.

650
00:50:40,165 --> 00:50:41,065
Thank you, Grandpa.

651
00:50:41,231 --> 00:50:42,031
Thank you, Grandma.

652
00:50:42,865 --> 00:50:43,665
Go on, dear.

653
00:50:43,865 --> 00:50:44,665
Isn't it heavy?

654
00:50:45,498 --> 00:50:46,555
I'll be waiting for you to eat.

655
00:50:46,555 --> 00:50:47,055
Okay.

656
00:50:47,055 --> 00:50:47,731
Just wait.

657
00:50:48,898 --> 00:50:49,698
It's going to be delicious.

658
00:50:51,231 --> 00:50:52,498
The fresh air here is wonderful.

659
00:50:53,465 --> 00:50:54,465
Come on, Grandma. Let's go.

660
00:50:55,731 --> 00:50:57,131
Watch your step, will you?

661
00:51:01,031 --> 00:51:03,498
This is where I spent my childhood.

662
00:51:06,231 --> 00:51:08,698
You suddenly brought me
all the way here.

663
00:51:09,698 --> 00:51:11,331
What's your plan exactly?

664
00:51:11,765 --> 00:51:12,565
Hmm?

665
00:51:12,698 --> 00:51:13,498
Nant.

666
00:51:13,565 --> 00:51:18,698
What plan, Boss? I just wanted to
show you around and enjoy nature.

667
00:51:21,098 --> 00:51:27,165
Really? Cause it's written all over
your face that you're up to something.

668
00:51:28,965 --> 00:51:30,231
What plan, Boss?

669
00:51:31,931 --> 00:51:36,442
I'm just teasing you. Since you brought
me here for a change of scenery,

670
00:51:36,442 --> 00:51:37,765
I don't mind at all.

671
00:51:40,331 --> 00:51:46,431
Nice view here.
So, what's interesting around?

672
00:51:47,698 --> 00:51:50,398
Over there, Boss.
Look over there.

673
00:51:50,398 --> 00:51:53,946
I used to play and run a proper
little shop here.

674
00:51:54,460 --> 00:51:55,219
Did you ever play like that, Boss?

675
00:51:55,961 --> 00:51:59,855
You know, back then, I'd use leaves...

676
00:51:59,855 --> 00:52:02,231
Big leaves, like these,
as money.

677
00:52:02,898 --> 00:52:04,465
Then I'd dig up some clay

678
00:52:04,698 --> 00:52:06,331
and mold it like this.

679
00:52:06,531 --> 00:52:07,186
Uh-huh.

680
00:52:07,186 --> 00:52:08,731
And now it's turn into little desserts.

681
00:52:08,898 --> 00:52:09,465
You know!

682
00:52:09,465 --> 00:52:12,265
I took running that
shop very seriously!

683
00:52:14,665 --> 00:52:17,831
Wait, a naughty girl like
you actually played that before?

684
00:52:18,831 --> 00:52:20,165
I can't picture it.

685
00:52:20,498 --> 00:52:21,775
Oh, Boss.

686
00:52:21,775 --> 00:52:22,275
Hmm?

687
00:52:22,498 --> 00:52:23,731
I was a kid once, you know.

688
00:52:24,631 --> 00:52:28,298
You're acting like
you were born all grown up.

689
00:52:29,965 --> 00:52:31,031
I was a kid too.

690
00:52:32,165 --> 00:52:34,642
But I never got to experience
life in the countryside,

691
00:52:35,270 --> 00:52:37,326
so I never had friends
to play these with.

692
00:52:38,753 --> 00:52:43,531
My childhood was spent staying within
the lines and going to extra classes.

693
00:52:46,331 --> 00:52:48,631
That's why you're so successful, Boss.

694
00:52:50,665 --> 00:52:51,731
Because you didn't waste time
messing around like me.

695
00:52:53,098 --> 00:52:53,898
Sigh...

696
00:52:54,698 --> 00:52:56,665
Honestly? I actually want
to play around a bit too.

697
00:52:58,931 --> 00:53:03,131
But not long after Chom was born,

698
00:53:04,631 --> 00:53:05,698
my father passed away.

699
00:53:07,565 --> 00:53:11,631
So I had to grow up quickly to be
there for my mom and sister.

700
00:53:20,331 --> 00:53:21,531
You're amazing, Boss.

701
00:53:23,365 --> 00:53:26,165
My Boss is the most amazing person
in the world.

702
00:53:42,731 --> 00:53:44,226
But...

703
00:53:45,710 --> 00:53:49,065
You didn't bring me here
for no reason, did you, Nant?

704
00:53:50,665 --> 00:53:51,465
Hmm?

705
00:53:52,231 --> 00:53:56,298
So, why exactly did you bring me here?

706
00:53:59,631 --> 00:54:00,431
I...

707
00:54:00,865 --> 00:54:02,098
There's really nothing, Boss.

708
00:54:03,265 --> 00:54:04,865
I told you already.

709
00:54:05,298 --> 00:54:06,765
I just missed my grandparents.

710
00:54:08,431 --> 00:54:09,531
There's nothing else.

711
00:54:10,765 --> 00:54:12,231
You're a terrible liar.

712
00:54:13,898 --> 00:54:15,331
Your eyes give you away.

713
00:54:16,898 --> 00:54:18,698
It's obvious
you're hiding something from me.

714
00:54:19,098 --> 00:54:21,331
Hmm? Why are you smiling,
you little brat?

715
00:54:23,031 --> 00:54:23,898
But that's okay.

716
00:54:25,131 --> 00:54:26,831
If you won't tell me nicely,

717
00:54:28,565 --> 00:54:29,765
I'll just have to force you.

718
00:54:30,365 --> 00:54:31,165
How?

719
00:54:32,431 --> 00:54:33,231
Like this.

720
00:54:36,165 --> 00:54:39,159
Boss, we're... we're outside!

721
00:54:39,159 --> 00:54:40,765
What if someone sees us?

722
00:54:42,031 --> 00:54:44,841
I don't care. So what?

723
00:54:45,469 --> 00:54:48,526
Is my way of forcing you scary?

724
00:54:53,765 --> 00:54:55,631
You're pretty funny, Boss.

725
00:54:58,498 --> 00:54:59,265
Boss.

726
00:54:59,265 --> 00:55:00,065
Hmm?

727
00:55:00,231 --> 00:55:01,331
What if one day...

728
00:55:01,698 --> 00:55:03,298
I really does something wrong?

729
00:55:05,465 --> 00:55:07,065
Will you be angry with me, Boss?

730
00:55:09,465 --> 00:55:10,831
If you do something wrong,

731
00:55:13,231 --> 00:55:14,765
I'll have to punish you.

732
00:55:17,865 --> 00:55:19,031
How will you punish me?

733
00:55:25,165 --> 00:55:25,965
Like this.

734
00:55:28,865 --> 00:55:30,531
This is how I punish naughty girls.

735
00:56:03,865 --> 00:56:05,631
Hey, Boss!
What are you taking pictures of?

736
00:56:06,931 --> 00:56:08,631
Just keeping some evidence.

737
00:56:09,131 --> 00:56:12,898
If you ever get on my nerves
or make me angry,

738
00:56:13,931 --> 00:56:16,065
I'll send these pictures
to the entire company.

739
00:56:17,031 --> 00:56:19,065
Boss, why would you...

740
00:56:20,265 --> 00:56:21,465
You're so mean.

741
00:56:22,365 --> 00:56:25,265
How am I supposed to dare
to do anything wrong now?

742
00:56:36,298 --> 00:56:37,431
You're so mean, Boss.

743
00:57:28,565 --> 00:57:29,282
Wait!

744
00:57:29,567 --> 00:57:31,846
Hey! Who turned off the lights?

745
00:57:33,765 --> 00:57:35,037
What are you doing, Nant?

746
00:57:45,765 --> 00:57:46,619
It's broken.

747
00:57:46,619 --> 00:57:47,217
Oh.

748
00:57:47,217 --> 00:57:47,717
Oh.

749
00:57:48,031 --> 00:57:48,965
I guess I used a little too much force.

750
00:57:49,531 --> 00:57:50,465
I've been working out.

751
00:57:51,498 --> 00:57:52,298
Uh...

752
00:57:53,465 --> 00:57:54,731
Boss, don't tell Grandma.

753
00:57:55,265 --> 00:57:56,065
Okay.

754
00:57:56,765 --> 00:57:58,331
Grandma will scold me.

755
00:58:00,531 --> 00:58:01,431
Let's keep this between us.

756
00:58:01,565 --> 00:58:02,365
Okay, okay.

757
00:58:26,498 --> 00:58:27,365
Thank you.

758
00:58:34,665 --> 00:58:36,365
Go ahead and eat first, dear.

759
00:58:36,831 --> 00:58:39,665
Grandma's going to make sure
Grandpa takes his medicine.

760
00:58:40,231 --> 00:58:40,731
Okay.

761
00:58:40,731 --> 00:58:41,331
Sure.

762
00:58:41,531 --> 00:58:42,331
Enjoy your meal.

763
00:58:43,365 --> 00:58:44,165
Thank you.

764
00:58:48,231 --> 00:58:49,665
Good thing Grandma didn't see that.

765
00:59:14,165 --> 00:59:14,929
Boss.

766
00:59:15,728 --> 00:59:16,685
Eat up.

767
00:59:17,370 --> 00:59:19,965
Grandma makes
the most delicious fried pork.

768
00:59:20,931 --> 00:59:21,731
Really?

769
00:59:23,265 --> 00:59:24,065
Boss.

770
00:59:24,131 --> 00:59:24,931
Hmm?

771
00:59:26,165 --> 00:59:27,131
What are you looking for?

772
00:59:28,131 --> 00:59:28,931
Uh...

773
00:59:29,765 --> 00:59:31,298
I can't find a spoon.

774
00:59:34,765 --> 00:59:35,565
Huh?

775
00:59:36,431 --> 00:59:37,465
You're eating sticky rice.

776
00:59:37,765 --> 00:59:39,165
Who eats that with a spoon?

777
00:59:40,065 --> 00:59:40,931
You eat sticky rice

778
00:59:41,731 --> 00:59:43,331
with your hands.

779
00:59:44,065 --> 00:59:44,865
Here.

780
00:59:45,831 --> 00:59:46,631
Come on.

781
00:59:46,731 --> 00:59:50,431
Let me give you
a little food presentation.

782
00:59:52,265 --> 00:59:53,065
Like this.

783
00:59:55,331 --> 00:59:56,131
Like this.

784
00:59:58,631 --> 01:00:01,631
A traditional-style omakase.

785
01:00:03,165 --> 01:00:03,831
Here.

786
01:00:03,831 --> 01:00:05,298
Boss, let me feed you.

787
01:00:05,665 --> 01:00:06,465
Open wide.

788
01:00:12,565 --> 01:00:14,003
Come on, open up.

789
01:00:14,003 --> 01:00:14,737
Have you washed your hands?

790
01:00:14,737 --> 01:00:15,813
I have.

791
01:00:19,238 --> 01:00:20,330
It's a little salty.

792
01:00:21,244 --> 01:00:21,992
So the pork is salty?

793
01:00:22,392 --> 01:00:23,145
Heh, it's my hands.

794
01:00:28,931 --> 01:00:29,731
How is it?

795
01:00:30,565 --> 01:00:31,365
Well...

796
01:00:32,165 --> 01:00:32,965
It's good.

797
01:00:33,965 --> 01:00:34,765
What?

798
01:00:35,465 --> 01:00:36,431
Just "good"?

799
01:00:37,498 --> 01:00:38,259
You're such a liar.

800
01:00:38,259 --> 01:00:38,831
Mm-hmm.

801
01:00:39,165 --> 01:00:41,531
You were nodding just now.

802
01:00:43,265 --> 01:00:44,331
It's delicious, isn't it?

803
01:00:45,331 --> 01:00:46,131
Mm-hmm.

804
01:00:47,765 --> 01:00:48,965
It's pretty good.

805
01:01:29,831 --> 01:01:30,582
Well...

806
01:01:32,066 --> 01:01:33,355
It's actually delicious.

807
01:02:03,331 --> 01:02:04,765
Come with me, please.

808
01:02:06,131 --> 01:02:06,931
I'm scared.

809
01:02:09,631 --> 01:02:11,098
Boss? Scared?

810
01:02:12,465 --> 01:02:15,765
Funny. When we were in bed,
you didn't seem scared at all.

811
01:02:17,231 --> 01:02:19,331
There's nothing to be afraid of, Boss.
Don't worry.

812
01:02:20,165 --> 01:02:20,965
Nothing's there.

813
01:02:24,365 --> 01:02:25,165
Okay.

814
01:02:25,631 --> 01:02:27,065
I'll just go shower by myself.

815
01:02:27,665 --> 01:02:29,165
I don't need you. Hmph.

816
01:02:32,898 --> 01:02:36,965
Hurry up. If you take too long,
the ghosts will get you.

817
01:02:41,865 --> 01:02:43,965
Walk too slowly and
the ghosts will grab your feet.

818
01:02:59,498 --> 01:03:01,106
Okay.

819
01:03:02,647 --> 01:03:03,931
Your phone.

820
01:03:10,898 --> 01:03:11,798
Boss.

821
01:03:12,369 --> 01:03:13,431
What's your phone password?

822
01:03:14,165 --> 01:03:15,265
Yeah, right, like I'd ever tell you.

823
01:03:16,231 --> 01:03:17,131
So possessive.

824
01:03:24,065 --> 01:03:24,898
Basic.

825
01:03:26,531 --> 01:03:27,631
It's definitely your birthday.

826
01:03:28,831 --> 01:03:31,831
You were born on January 18th.

827
01:03:35,231 --> 01:03:36,665
One-eight-zero-one.

828
01:03:42,965 --> 01:03:44,365
Damn it, that's not it.

829
01:03:44,965 --> 01:03:45,865
Then what is it?

830
01:03:46,965 --> 01:03:48,665
Gregorian year? Buddhist year?

831
01:03:50,098 --> 01:03:51,098
Probably not.

832
01:04:00,165 --> 01:04:05,698
Don't tell me your passcode
is some boomer code.

833
01:04:07,522 --> 01:04:08,266
Two.

834
01:04:08,551 --> 01:04:09,352
Three.

835
01:04:10,323 --> 01:04:11,295
Four.

836
01:04:11,606 --> 01:04:13,606
Wait!

837
01:04:17,965 --> 01:04:18,765
Boss.

838
01:04:19,131 --> 01:04:20,765
That's such an old-fashioned password.

839
01:04:24,365 --> 01:04:27,631
Let's see this camera of yours.
Is the quality any good?

840
01:04:36,465 --> 01:04:37,265
Let's see.

841
01:04:39,465 --> 01:04:42,098
Why don't
I look as pretty as Boss?

842
01:04:49,465 --> 01:04:50,265
Hey!

843
01:04:50,865 --> 01:04:52,831
Where did she get that photo?

844
01:04:59,631 --> 01:05:00,131
Hey!

845
01:05:00,131 --> 01:05:00,931
Hey!

846
01:05:01,165 --> 01:05:01,965
What?

847
01:05:02,165 --> 01:05:03,665
Were you snooping through my phone?

848
01:05:04,431 --> 01:05:05,231
Boss.

849
01:05:05,831 --> 01:05:09,165
Why do you have so many pictures of me
saved on your phone?

850
01:05:09,565 --> 01:05:10,731
Uh... Well...

851
01:05:12,898 --> 01:05:18,036
I... I only saved them for blackmail.

852
01:05:19,806 --> 01:05:24,902
So I could send them to everyone
at the company if you misbehave.

853
01:05:29,331 --> 01:05:30,131
Boss.

854
01:05:30,898 --> 01:05:31,698
Hmm?

855
01:05:34,431 --> 01:05:36,265
Can you swear

856
01:05:38,731 --> 01:05:39,698
that you...

857
01:05:42,765 --> 01:05:44,331
have never used
my pictures for anything else?

858
01:05:47,973 --> 01:05:48,888
Hmm?

859
01:06:04,698 --> 01:06:06,698
Let me be your first, okay?

860
01:06:41,498 --> 01:06:42,831
Your first time...

861
01:06:44,298 --> 01:06:45,565
belongs to me now.

862
01:07:12,665 --> 01:07:16,750
Oh, Chat.
Why is your face so red, dear?

863
01:07:17,207 --> 01:07:18,422
Do you have a fever?

864
01:07:20,765 --> 01:07:21,565
No, Grandma.

865
01:07:23,631 --> 01:07:24,765
It's just hot.

866
01:07:25,098 --> 01:07:25,831
Really?

867
01:07:25,831 --> 01:07:26,698
Hot. Very hot.

868
01:07:27,031 --> 01:07:27,831
I'm sweating.

869
01:07:27,931 --> 01:07:30,298
But I think it's quite cold in here.

870
01:07:30,898 --> 01:07:31,698
Mm-hmm.

871
01:07:31,898 --> 01:07:32,698
Right.

872
01:07:33,465 --> 01:07:34,765
I thinks it's freezing, too.

873
01:07:35,698 --> 01:07:37,365
I've got goosebumps all over.

874
01:07:38,731 --> 01:07:39,698
Uh... Uh...

875
01:07:40,131 --> 01:07:41,831
Excuse me, Grandma.

876
01:07:52,331 --> 01:07:55,565
So, is it hot or cold, Nant?

877
01:07:56,465 --> 01:07:57,431
I have no idea, Grandma.

878
01:08:00,965 --> 01:08:04,898
Grandma, can I sleep with you tonight?

879
01:08:07,898 --> 01:08:08,698
No way.

880
01:08:09,065 --> 01:08:10,231
You're better off sleeping over there.

881
01:08:10,498 --> 01:08:14,298
You're all grown up now. Why squeeze
in with me? I'll feel cramped.

882
01:08:14,731 --> 01:08:15,531
Come on.

883
01:08:16,698 --> 01:08:17,498
I promise

884
01:08:18,031 --> 01:08:20,931
I'll make myself as small
as I was when I was little.

885
01:08:21,631 --> 01:08:24,131
Please let me sleep with you.

886
01:08:29,231 --> 01:08:33,065
Are you really going to leave
your girlfriend sleeping all alone?

887
01:08:33,865 --> 01:08:37,298
Oh, it's fine, Grandma. She
can sleep by herself.

888
01:08:38,231 --> 01:08:39,031
Hahaha.

889
01:08:39,765 --> 01:08:40,965
Hey! No, that's not it!

890
01:08:42,231 --> 01:08:43,498
She's not my girlfriend.

891
01:08:43,898 --> 01:08:45,565
She is my boss.

892
01:08:46,265 --> 01:08:49,098
Oh, so she's not your girlfriend.

893
01:08:50,511 --> 01:08:52,511
But she's your husband.

894
01:08:53,321 --> 01:08:54,965
Whoa!

895
01:08:54,965 --> 01:08:56,298
That's quite something, Grandma.

896
01:08:58,065 --> 01:09:00,990
Alright, alright.
If she's not, then she's not.

897
01:09:01,732 --> 01:09:05,031
By the way, did you see your mother
while you were there?

898
01:09:09,231 --> 01:09:10,265
No, I didn't.

899
01:09:16,365 --> 01:09:19,031
Is Grandpa asleep already?

900
01:09:20,931 --> 01:09:22,098
Your grandpa?

901
01:09:23,365 --> 01:09:25,231
He's glued to his phone all the time.

902
01:09:25,865 --> 01:09:28,531
Whoa, that is totally unacceptable.
Unacceptable.

903
01:09:29,698 --> 01:09:34,265
I'll go scold that naughty man
after I finish showering.

904
01:09:35,365 --> 01:09:36,631
Why won't he go to bed?

905
01:09:37,298 --> 01:09:40,031
I'll go take a shower first, Grandma.

906
01:09:40,298 --> 01:09:41,098
Alright, dear.

907
01:09:41,831 --> 01:09:43,465
I need to go scold that naughty man.

908
01:10:02,865 --> 01:10:03,919
So...

909
01:10:05,575 --> 01:10:08,921
What kind of person
is Nant's mother, anyway?

910
01:12:22,765 --> 01:12:24,331
What the hell is going on here?

911
01:12:24,531 --> 01:12:25,731
You have to take responsibility!

912
01:12:26,165 --> 01:12:28,031
The total comes to 25,000.

913
01:12:28,465 --> 01:12:29,265
From now on,

914
01:12:29,631 --> 01:12:31,898
I don't want you doing anything
dangerous like that again.

915
01:12:32,331 --> 01:12:34,331
Then where am I supposed
to get the money?

916
01:12:36,365 --> 01:12:37,165
From me.

917
01:12:39,131 --> 01:12:42,231
Let me be...the only one who hires you.
